<title>EGYPT: Egypt YR/YR money supply up 12.5 pct in Feb 97.</title>
<headline>Egypt YR/YR money supply up 12.5 pct in Feb 97.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian broad money supply grew 12.5 percent in the year ending February 1997, from 12.9 percent in the year to January 1997, the Central Bank of Egypt said in a bulletin.</p>
<p>Total money supply, including quasi-money and foreign currency deposits, was 181.302 billion pounds at end-February 1997 against 180.089 billion at end-January.</p>
<p>Following figures, all in billions, were supplied by the Central Bank.</p>
<p>					  Feb 97    Jan 97    Feb 96</p>
<p>    Total money supply	   181.302   180.089   161.125</p>
<p>    Money			     37.505    38.018    34.335</p>
<p>    Quasi-money		    143.797   142.071   126.790</p>
<p>    Year-on-year growth (pct)   +12.5     +12.9	 --</p>
<p>    Month-on-month growth (pct) +0.67     +0.83	0.99</p>
<p>The Central Bank figures differ slightly from those published by the International Monetary Fund.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
